  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Result (output) 2.1 
Girls and boys including children with disability have access to Child Friendly spaces (CFSs) &amp; resilience program</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="276315" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN"># of girls and boys are benefitting from the PSS support provided in Child Friendly Spaces</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="n/a"></target>
     <actual value="SCI &#x2013; AF established 14 CFSs through which provided psychosocial support, to 1010 children (girls 508, boys 502) between the ages of 5 and 9

252 youths (127 male, 125 female) and 250 children (125 boys, 125 girls) successfully completed youth and child resilience workshop in both target provinces."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objective 1: Vulnerable households in Nangarhar and Kunduz are enabled to better cope with economic shocks and natural disasters.</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="272968" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">% of targeted households report sustained and liveable income as a result of project.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="n/a"></target>
     <actual value="The socioeconomic empowerment of marginalized returnees, IDPs and host communities was increased through improved livelihood opportunities. Through community-based capital building, 2002 households received support, and income generating activities (IGA) were provided to those with at least one business relevant skill. In addition, micro-enterprise activities were prioritized for women to expand home-based self-employment and ear a regular income. The employment and micro-enterprise activities were identified through localized labour market assessment. Furthermore, 1002 youths from returnee and IDP communities graduated from vocational training and received graduation certificates and start up tools as well as guidance on market linkages."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objective 2: Girls and boys are protected from violence, abuse, exploitation and neglect with access to psychosocial support, case management and referral services</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="276314" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">% of targeted households report sustained and liveable income as a result of project.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="n/a"></target>
     <actual value="This project has improved target communities&#x2019; knowledge on child protection and child rights, especially parents, caregivers, teachers, and community elders were targeted. Sc staff has observed that this has contributed to a reduction in violence against children. SC has established 14 Child Friendly Spaces (CFSs) and registered 1010 children, who have all received psychosocial support through recreational activities. 345 child cases were identified and managed. 
 
The youth and child resilience activities were initiated based on non-clinical, psychosocial and protection methodologies and focus on children&#x2019;s positive coping and resilience. Within this activity 502 children and youths participated, building their social resilience and well-being. 495 parents (264 mothers and 231 fathers) also participated in child and youth resilience activities."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
